Subject: [PATCH 08029/11362] The noise floor was measured on one arm of a
 two-arm comparison; measured the other, and the finding survives

An 11-item adversarial review of the composite treatment-activation pre-flight. Two findings
changed a number, one needed a fresh GPU measurement to settle, and two were wrong on their
specifics and are recorded as corrections rather than quietly adopted.

The one that needed a measurement. The grid reported an "A/A noise floor" of 0/6, but that is the
HEAD arm's floor (head vs headb) while every A/B pair is base-vs-head and holds one unreplicated
base run. The review's hypothesis -- base is the noisy arm, collapsing the attributable count 4 to
1 -- had real supporting evidence: the base worktree's own proto_just_explore_budget_scan.json
documents the explore path as nondeterministic across fresh processes via hash-keyed frontier
iteration, and probe_cell.py pins no PYTHONHASHSEED. Ran a baseb arm on the four attributable
cells: base vs baseb IDENTICAL on all four (tu93 28/28, tr87 27/27, tn36 31/31, vc33 14/14),
base-arm floor 0/4. Refuted by measurement; the count stands at 4. Stated as a limit, not a
reassurance -- this is about these cells at budget=60, not a proof the channel is closed.

The instrument was fixed too, not just the artifact. preflight_verdict accepted one noise_pairs
mapping and treated it as certifying a comparison spanning two arms, so a grid whose CONTROL arm
was the noisy one would credit the control's self-perturbation to the treatment. It now takes
noise_pairs_b; attribution requires every supplied mapping to witness the cell, an absent cell is
unwitnessed rather than passed, and a single-arm call warns. 8 new tests, 36 existing ones pass.

A compute-bound artifact could omit duration_s and pass the duration check in silence.
check_duration_vs_claim returns immediately on a non-finite duration, so an artifact declaring
live_llm_inference with duration_s: null was reported clean -- verified by injection, 1.0 and
0.0001 fire CRITICAL and null passes. Strictly worse than a short duration: omitting the field
makes a fabricator invisible to the check built to catch them. Fixed in check_methodology_present,
which already gates on the right population. Corpus impact measured over all 6311 artifacts before
shipping: 656 gain the string inside a warn they already carried, ZERO acquire a new warn.

Two review items were wrong. (1) "2 of 3 A/B truncations dropped the head cell" -- sc25's truncated
arm is headb, which is in the A/A arm; of the two A/B events one dropped head and one dropped base,
symmetric. The broader point survives weaker and is recorded: head is 2.5-3.1x slower on exactly
the two cells where the treatment activates. (2) "Every A/A pair spanned both GPUs" was indeed
false, but the count is 7 of 8, not 5 of 6.

Four reporting-basis corrections: the Fisher table compared mismatched cell sets and counted cd82
when it helped while excluding it when it did not (now 4/5 vs 0/5, p=0.0238 primary, with the
shared-head-arm dependence disclosed); structural_channel_check's "guaranteed identical" claim was
falsified by its own data and is retracted, splitting attributable-to-span (4) from
attributable-to-induction (1); a stale "truncation count is 0" sentence was the stated
justification for dismissing a CRITICAL flag and is now computed; duration_s recorded.

A fourth instance of the same comparator bug, found by review: the external/native cross-check
compared the string "None" against a genuine absent payload, reporting disagreement at index 1-2
while the prose correctly said the recorders agree. Fixed and extended; all 14 cells now agree.
Four independent instances in one session of "no value" treated as "a value".

Also: the mutation guard whose advice destroys work. --check answered "which tracked files
changed?" then printed git checkout -- over the union as though it had answered "which files did
the run write?". The prior survey called this unfixable because the two are identical at the FILE
level; they are distinct at the PROCESS level, and the damage mechanism is in-process, so an audit
hook observes it directly. Replayed against the 6-file incident: pre-fix destroys 6/6, post-fix
destroys 0/6 and still restores the genuine artifact rewrite. Five further defects found while
building it, including xdist workers going unobserved under the default -n 4.

Verdicts. The code changes the live agent: yes, 4 of 7 usable cells, but only 1 where the induction
channel was open. Banked levels unchanged at 3/3 -- no banked-levels grid was run. Submission gate
NOT met, and mis-calibrated: the real leaderboard is 0.08 three times and 0.12 once.

No submission was made or staged and no scored or online ARC game was played.

