+    "why_it_did_not_bite_here_stated_as_a_limit_not_a_reassurance": "the documented nondeterminism is in the just-explore GRAPH EXPLORER's frontier. This probe runs the E3AgentPolicy explore stream at budget=60 with explore_budget=24, and on these four cells that stream is evidently reproducible across processes. That is an empirical result about THESE cells at THIS budget, not a proof that the channel is closed: a different game, a longer budget, or a path that reaches the graph explorer could still expose it. Any future grid should pin PYTHONHASHSEED on both arms rather than rely on this holding.",
+    "why_this_field_exists": "the grid's original 'A/A floor' was head-vs-headb ONLY. Every A/B pair is base-vs-head and holds exactly ONE base run, unreplicated -- so a 0/6 head-arm floor proves HEAD repeats itself and says NOTHING about BASE. If base is the noisy arm, the perturbations credited to the treatment are the base arm perturbing against itself. That is not a hypothetical: 4f7e5f55a changes the search's dedup KEY, exactly the kind of change that can STABILISE iteration order, so a determinism ASYMMETRY between the arms is the EXPECTED consequence of the treatment. probe_cell.py also never pins PYTHONHASHSEED, so str/bytes hashing is randomised per process on both arms. Measured rather than assumed."
