+      "CONFIRMED_BY_THE_FLAG_CLEARING_ITSELF": "the cleanest possible proof, and it arrived without touching a single number. On the 4-game and 6-game builds the A/B arm had ZERO truncation-affected cells, charitable ceiling == strict ceiling, and the flag fired. On the FINAL 8-game build su15's A/B came back TRUNCATION_ONLY, so charitable = strict + 1 = 5 vs strict 4, the two p-values separated (0.0625 vs 0.125), and adversarial_verify now reports '0 flagged'. The flag appeared and disappeared exactly as the slack term went 0 -> 1, which is what a structural identity does and what a real two-metric bug would not.",
