+  "grid_design_finding_the_threshold_assumes_all_12_cells_are_usable": {
+    "claim": "the '6 one-way discordant pairs out of 12 cells' threshold silently assumes all 12 cells YIELD a usable observation. On this path some do not, so the effective denominator is smaller than 12 and the required attributable RATE is higher than the 50% the '6 of 12' framing suggests.",
+    "confirmed_in_this_run_not_only_predicted": "sc25's A/A replicate hit the 1500s hard timeout and was SIGTERM'd mid-induction (status blocked_hard_timeout_sigterm, 26 actions of partial trace), so sc25's A/A is TRUNCATION_ONLY and the cell is excluded from the A/A denominator. Its base and head cells took 1100s and 1150s against a 1200s wall cap -- i.e. the cell was already at the edge, and the third arm fell off it. The truncation risk is therefore not a prediction transplanted from the retention grid; it materialised here, on the FOURTH game, before the grid even reached the games known to be slower.",
+    "consequence": "if k of 12 cells are truncation-affected, the sign test needs 6 of (12-k) usable cells to be attributably perturbed. At k=2 that is 60%; at k=5 (the retention grid's rate) it is 86%, which no plausible treatment reaches. So a 12-game grid on the slow games is close to arithmetically undesignable, independent of the treatment.",
+    "evidence_from_the_prior_retention_grid": "in results/arc_engine_retention_20260729, cn04 and r11l were BOTH_TRUNCATED (both arms cut off at 26-28 of a 400-action budget) and lp85, ls20, su15 were TRUNCATION_ONLY -- 5 of 12 cells truncation-affected, leaving 7 usable. The pre-flight correctly EXCLUDES those as missing observations rather than scoring them zero, which is right -- but it means the grid never had 12 chances.",
+    "recommendation": "size the grid by USABLE cells, not scheduled cells: either drop the games that reliably truncate at this wall-clock cap, raise the cap for them specifically, or schedule enough extra games that the expected usable count clears the threshold. This is a design fix, not a re-analysis -- no amount of care in the analysis can recover power the schedule never had.",
+    "status_in_this_run": "see ab_class_counts / n_truncation_affected for the running totals. Reported as a design finding regardless of this run's outcome, because the arithmetic gap exists whether or not this particular grid tripped over it."
+  },
