+  "structural_channel_check": {
+    "RETRACTION_the_guaranteed_identical_claim_was_WRONG": "the first version of this field said that on a cell where NEITHER arm found a plan 'the two arms are GUARANTEED to emit identical traces however differently they induced'. That is false, and this artifact's own numbers falsified it: tn36, tr87 and tu93 are ALL in cells_with_no_plan_on_either_arm AND all three are classified PERTURBED, diverging at action index 2-3. Both facts were stated and never reconciled. The claim was wrong because it conflated the INDUCTION channel with the ACTION STREAM: a plan is the only route from an induction-side change to the actions, but the EXPLORE stream runs whether or not a plan is ever found, and a change to hashing, dedup or tie-breaking reorders it directly. The correct statement is narrower: on a no-plan cell the INDUCTION channel is closed, so any perturbation observed there is NOT evidence for the induction-side fixes -- it is evidence that SOMETHING in the 25-commit span reordered exploration.",
